{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And you shall say to them: I am YHWH your Elohim.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): 'And you shall say to them in My name'; thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory." "<b>By way of the Midrash:</b> 'I am YHWH your Elohim' — I am the One who said at Sinai, ״אנכי ה׳ אלהיך״ ('I am YHWH your Elohim,' Exodus 20:2), and you accepted My divinity upon yourselves; from now on accept My decrees. Rabbi says: It was revealed and known before Him that they would ultimately falter in forbidden relations in the days of Ezra; therefore He came upon them with the decree 'I am YHWH your Elohim' — He is a judge to exact payment and faithful to pay reward." "<b>By way of the Kabbalah:</b> 'I am YHWH your Elohim' — not a word is missing, but it is as it is written plainly, for the Elohim of Israel — that is 'I,' as it says (Exodus 25:9) ״ככל אשר אני״ ('according to all that I'), and likewise (Exodus 15:26) ״כי אני ה׳ רפאך״ ('for I am YHWH your healer')."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:26:11.120940050Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}